## Third-party data

The MIT terms above cover this project's own source. The bundled dictionary and
frequency data is licensed separately by its authors, is not relicensed here,
and keeps its own terms:

- `cedict_ts.u8`, `cedict.json`, and the Android SQLite asset generated from them
  derive from CC-CEDICT (https://cc-cedict.org/), licensed CC BY-SA 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). The generated files are
  adaptations, so they carry the same attribution and share-alike terms.

- `subtlex_ch.tsv` derives from SUBTLEX-CH — Cai Q, Brysbaert M (2010),
  "SUBTLEX-CH: Chinese Word and Character Frequencies Based on Film Subtitles",
  PLoS ONE 5(6): e10729 — licensed CC BY
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Trimmed to headword and
  occurrences per million; no other change.
